<title>USA: Arrhythmia acquires Astro-Med line.</title>
<headline>Arrhythmia acquires Astro-Med line.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arrhythmia Research Technology Inc said Wednesday it acquired from Astro-Med Inc the K-3 product family of hemodynamic systems for cardiac catheterization laboratories.</p>
<p>The company said it has been the exclusive distributor in the U.S., Canada, Eastern Block countries and Russia since December 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;The K-3 cath lab recorder line will now be sold worldwide by Arrhythmia,&quot; the company said.</p>
</text>
